@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
skinparam ArrowColor #CBD5E1
title Proposed environment separation — contexts, not three new paid hosts
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Identified versioned release / dependency / schema manifest" as R
node "Development context" {
 artifact "Local controlled app / tests" as DEV
 database "Synthetic development state" as DD
 DEV --> DD
}
node "Isolated staging / recovery rehearsal context\nFacility pending; may be temporary" {
 artifact "Candidate release + guarded workers" as ST
 database "Controlled compatible state / restricted keys" as SD
 ST --> SD
}
node "Production candidate context\nActual promotion/readiness pending" {
 artifact "Reviewed exact release + configuration identity" as PR
 database "Authorized operating state / private artifacts" as PD
 PR --> PD
}
R --> DEV
R --> ST
R --> PR : only reviewed promotion
legend bottom
 Separate data/credentials/addresses and outbound-effect controls are required in each actual facility.
 A database name or namespace alone is not sufficient isolation; staging must not send/deploy with production credentials.
 Production data is not copied into dev/staging by default; no automatic database promotion is implied.
endlegend
@enduml
